#
# hpcperfstatsd site overrides (example; tracked)
#
# Copy to site/hpcperfstats.site.conf in this checkout (gitignored, never committed), set the
# values for your site, and chmod 0600 it. The RPM build lays these keys over the repo default
# src/hpcperfstats.conf: a key the default has gets its value replaced in place, any other key
# is appended. Same syntax as hpcperfstats.conf (`key value`; ':' or '=' also separate).
#
# Fleet prepares (prepare_rpmbuild_stampede3.sh / _ls6.sh / _horizon.sh) refuse to build when
# the effective `server` is empty or localhost (opt out: HPCS_ALLOW_DEFAULT_BROKER=1).
#
# Do not edit src/hpcperfstats.conf or hpcperfstats.spec on node checkouts; put site settings
# here. The file is copied into the source tarball and SRPM under rpmbuild/, so keep that tree
# private too.

server   rabbitmq.example.org
queue    CLUSTER_QUEUE
port     5672
user     MONITOR_USER
password MONITOR_PASSWORD

# Any other hpcperfstats.conf key may be overridden the same way, for example:
# jobid_file /var/run/stats_jobid
# buffer_hours 6
